WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:05.214
That morning the diner was extra busy.

2
00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:17.364
Ally, Flo, and Barry dashed from table to table taking orders, and Randy and Ray cooked nonstop in the kitchen.

3
00:00:17.365 --> 00:00:22.085
"There are so many unfamiliar faces in here," Ally said to Flo.

4
00:00:22.086 --> 00:00:26.003
"Are they all bird-watchers in town to look for the whoopers?"

5
00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:33.474
"They don't look like bird-watchers to me," Flo replied. "They'd have binoculars and field guides."

6
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:36.520
"Maybe there's a convention," Ally said.

7
00:00:36.521 --> 00:00:45.065
"I'll ask those people at table five before I take their order."

8
00:00:45.066 --> 00:00:51.663
"Hi, folks, welcome to Ray's," Ally said. "What brings you all to town?"

9
00:00:51.664 --> 00:00:54.777
"We're here looking for a scoop," a tall man replied.

10
00:00:54.778 --> 00:01:01.596
"Oh, so you want ice cream for breakfast?" Ally asked. "We have vanilla, chocolate . . ."

11
00:01:01.597 --> 00:01:07.832
"No!" The man laughed. "We're reporters, so a scoop for us is a big news story.

12
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:11.978
We're here to cover Lainie Polk's P.O.D. launch."

13
00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:17.720
"The rumors are true? Lainie Polk is launching her P.O.D. from Sandville?"

14
00:01:17.721 --> 00:01:20.686
Ally could hardly contain her excitement.

15
00:01:20.687 --> 00:01:23.971
"Do you know when? How many passengers can she take?"

16
00:01:23.972 --> 00:01:29.511
"Hold up! We're usually the ones who ask the questions!" the reporter said.

17
00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:31.788
"Sorry, that's all the information we have right now.

18
00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:39.521
But if Lainie Polk does show up in town, we'll be standing by, waiting to cover the story."

19
00:01:39.522 --> 00:01:42.420
Ally had trouble concentrating as she worked.

20
00:01:42.421 --> 00:01:47.766
All she could think about was getting back to a planet in her own solar system.

21
00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:54.165
"As long as we land on an inhabited planet, I'll find a comm device and call my parents.

22
00:01:54.166 --> 00:01:58.893
Gosh, I have so much to tell them. I won't even know where to begin."

23
00:01:58.894 --> 00:02:02.903
"Excuse me," a customer at the counter called.

24
00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:08.382
"Do you have any cupcakes today, or did they all fall on the floor?"

25
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:12.723
Ally was confused until she recognized the customer.

26
00:02:12.724 --> 00:02:19.449
It was the woman from the other day, the one who'd caught the tray of cupcakes.

27
00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:27.016
"Oh, hi again." Ally smiled. "Are you in town for Lainie Polk's announcement too?"

28
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:29.320
The customer shook her head.

29
00:02:29.321 --> 00:02:35.692
"It sure seems like everyone else is, doesn't it?"

30
00:02:35.693 --> 00:02:43.485
She looked closely at Ally. "Are you interested in space travel?"

31
00:02:43.486 --> 00:02:49.802
"Yes!" Ally exclaimed. "It's the only way I'll ever get home again!"

32
00:02:49.803 --> 00:02:54.043
She gasped and slapped her hand over her mouth.

33
00:02:54.044 --> 00:02:57.122
"Why did I say that out loud?" she thought.

34
00:02:57.123 --> 00:03:01.326
"It's almost like that customer made me say it!"

35
00:03:01.327 --> 00:03:06.734
That's when Ally remembered the difference between Carparians and Camparians.

36
00:03:06.735 --> 00:03:11.478
"Carparians are shape-shifters," Ally's teacher had explained.

37
00:03:11.479 --> 00:03:16.348
"They have the power to make others tell the truth just by looking in their eyes.

38
00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:20.321
But Carparians are very different from Astralians.

39
00:03:20.322 --> 00:03:29.871
They are an aggressive species who enjoy creating mayhem, not peace, on other planets."

40
00:03:29.872 --> 00:03:35.593
"Um . . ." Ally gulped and avoided making eye contact with the customer.

41
00:03:35.594 --> 00:03:40.957
"I think I hear Ray calling me in the kitchen. I'll be right back."

42
00:03:40.958 --> 00:03:44.297
Ally scurried into the kitchen and grabbed Barry.

43
00:03:44.298 --> 00:03:45.793
"I have to make a phone call.

44
00:03:45.794 --> 00:03:48.805
Can you please take the order of that customer at the counter?"

45
00:03:48.806 --> 00:03:52.771
"Sure thing," Barry said.

46
00:03:52.772 --> 00:03:57.851
Ally ducked behind the door and watched as Barry took the customer's order.

47
00:03:57.852 --> 00:04:06.423
"If she is a Carparian," Ally thought, "maybe she'll make Barry blurt something out too!"

48
00:04:06.424 --> 00:04:11.835
But the customer simply gave Barry her order and then went back to reading on her phone.

49
00:04:11.836 --> 00:04:19.203
Ally sighed in relief. "There was nothing strange about her interaction with Barry," she told herself.

50
00:04:19.204 --> 00:04:27.180
"My imagination is working overtime again."

51
00:04:27.181 --> 00:04:29.745
Ally headed back into the dining room.

52
00:04:29.746 --> 00:04:34.578
Ping! Ping! Ping! Just then all the customers' phones began pinging.

53
00:04:34.579 --> 00:04:40.521
Everyone, except for the woman at the counter, got up and rushed for the door.

54
00:04:40.522 --> 00:04:45.404
Ally stopped the tall reporter on his way out. "What's going on?"

55
00:04:45.405 --> 00:04:49.801
"Lainie Polk is holding a press conference at the UFO Museum in an hour," he said.

56
00:04:49.802 --> 00:04:55.710
"I knew she was in Sandville, and I'm never wrong!" He rushed out the door.

57
00:04:55.711 --> 00:05:00.101
"In one hour?" Ally thought, looking at the clock.

58
00:05:00.102 --> 00:05:06.507
She still had three hours left on her shift, but she had to get to that press conference.

59
00:05:06.508 --> 00:05:10.746
"Flo, can you cover for me for a few hours?" Ally asked.

60
00:05:10.747 --> 00:05:18.588
Flo shrugged. "No problem. We were really busy before, but now this place is practically empty."

61
00:05:18.589 --> 00:05:24.583
"Thanks, I owe you one!" Ally took off her apron and ran outside to call Mateo.

62
00:05:24.584 --> 00:05:28.173
Before she could dial his number, her own phone rang.

63
00:05:28.174 --> 00:05:37.787
It was Mateo. "Meet me at the museum—as fast as you can!"

